  {
   "id": "bW3uiFo-41sJ",
   "from": "Vince S. Buffalo",
   "author": "b35e99045f6c74c2",
   "date": "2015-01-10T23:10:50Z",
   "subject": "Re: [D-RUG]: reassignment within mapply?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Bonnie,<div><br></div><div>I think I see a few issues here. First your mapply() needs to return something (not just attempt to modify the dataframe which won&#39;t work due to scoping rules) — preferably the modified dataframe. Second, a usual suspect with mappy() is by default the argument SIMPLIFY=TRUE, which almost always makes one&#39;s life not simple. </div><div><br></div><div>Admittedly I&#39;m not 100% sure what you&#39;re doing here, but it seems you want to have (1) a dataframe of changes to be made by row, column, and new value, and (2) apply these changes to the same dataframe storing the different versions in a list. So here&#39;s what I&#39;d do:</div><div><br></div><div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">&gt; dat &lt;- data.frame(ID = c(1, 2, 3, 4, 5),</font></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">+                   V1 = rep(5, 5),</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">+                   V2 = rep(7, 5),</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">+                   V3 = rep(6, 5))</font></div></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">&gt; # some fake changes, but kept tidy in a dataframe:</font></div><div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">&gt; changes &lt;- data.frame(row=sample(1:nrow(dat), 3), col=sample(2:4, 3), new.value=runif(3))</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">&gt; changes</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">  row col new.value</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">1   3   4 0.9469917</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">2   2   3 0.4958510</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">3   1   2 0.3440302</font></div></div><div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">&gt; with(changes, mapply(function(r, c, v) {dat[r, c] &lt;- v; dat}, row, col, new.value, SIMPLIFY=FALSE))</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">[[1]]</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">  ID V1 V2        V3</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">1  1  5  7 6.0000000</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">2  2  5  7 6.0000000</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">3  3  5  7 0.9469917</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">4  4  5  7 6.0000000</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">5  5  5  7 6.0000000</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">[[2]]</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">  ID V1       V2 V3</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">1  1  5 7.000000  6</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">2  2  5 0.495851  6</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">3  3  5 7.000000  6</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">4  4  5 7.000000  6</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">5  5  5 7.000000  6</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">[[3]]</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">  ID        V1 V2 V3</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">1  1 0.3440302  7  6</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">2  2 5.0000000  7  6</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">3  3 5.0000000  7  6</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">4  4 5.0000000  7  6</font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\">5  5 5.0000000  7  6</font></div></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"monospace, monospace\"><br></font></div>Is that what you&#39;re looking for?<div><br></div><div>HTH,<div>Vince</div></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Sat, Jan 10, 2015 at 2:48 PM, Bonnie Dixon <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">bonnie...@gmail.com</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Dear D-RUG folks;</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Here is a data manipulation task, which I would like to automate, so as to do it within a function.  I have a data frame, like this one, in which all the values in each column are identical except the ID variable.</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248);white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">dat &lt;- data.frame(ID = c(1, 2, 3, 4, 5),\r\n                  V1 = rep(5, 5),\r\n                  V2 = rep(7, 5),\r\n                  V3 = rep(6, 5))\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">I need to make several different versions of this data frame, each with one column changed to a different value (all values in the column still identical).  I have a vector listing the names of the columns to be changed, and a vector listing the new values for each column.</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248);white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">col.names &lt;- c(&quot;V1&quot;, &quot;V3&quot;)\r\nnew.values &lt;- c(4, 8)\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">The final result I am hoping to achieve would be a list of the new versions of the data frame, each with the appropriate column changed to its new value, like this:</p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248);white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">new.dat &lt;- \r\n  list(data.frame(ID = c(1, 2, 3, 4, 5),\r\n                  V1 = rep(4, 5),\r\n                  V2 = rep(7, 5),\r\n                  V3 = rep(6, 5)),\r\n       data.frame(ID = c(1, 2, 3, 4, 5),\r\n                  V1 = rep(5, 5),\r\n                  V2 = rep(7, 5),\r\n                  V3 = rep(8, 5)))\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">In attempting to automate this task, here is what I have tried.  I created a list of as many copies of the original data frame as there are elements in the vector naming the columns to be changed.  Then I attempted to use an mapply statement to reassign the specified columns to their new values.  But this did not work as intended.  </p>\r\n<pre style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;font-size:1em;line-height:1.2em;margin:1.2em 0px\"><code style=\"font-size:0.85em;font-family:Consolas,Inconsolata,Courier,monospace;margin:0px 0.15em;padding:0px 0.3em;white-space:pre-wrap;border:1px solid rgb(234,234,234);border-radius:3px;display:inline;background-color:rgb(248,248,248);white-space:pre-wrap;overflow:auto;border-radius:3px;border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding:0.5em 0.7em;display:block!important\">list.dat &lt;- lapply(col.names, function(x) {dat})\r\n\r\nlist.dat2 &lt;- \r\n  mapply(function(x, y, z) \r\n           {x[y] &lt;- z},\r\n         list.dat,\r\n         col.names,\r\n         new.values)\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">I think the problem is that you cannot reassign a column within an mapply statement like that.  But I am not sure how to rewrite this to accomplish my objective.  Any help would be greatly appreciated.</p>\r\n<p style=\"margin:1.2em 0px!important\">Bonnie</p>\r\n<div title=\"MDH:PGRpdj5EZWFyIEQtUlVHIGZvbGtzOzwvZGl2PjxkaXY+PGJyPjwvZGl2PjxkaXY+SGVyZSBpcyBh\r\nIGRhdGEgbWFuaXB1bGF0aW9uIHRhc2ssIHdoaWNoIEkgd291bGQgbGlrZSB0byBhdXRvbWF0ZSwg\r\nc28gYXMgdG8gZG8gaXQgd2l0aGluIGEgZnVuY3Rpb24uICZuYnNwO0kgaGF2ZSBhIGRhdGEgZnJh\r\nbWUsIGxpa2UgdGhpcyBvbmUsIGluIHdoaWNoIGFsbCB0aGUgdmFsdWVzIGluIGVhY2ggY29sdW1u\r\nIGFyZSBpZGVudGljYWwgZXhjZXB0IHRoZSBJRCB2YXJpYWJsZS48L2Rpdj48ZGl2Pjxicj48L2Rp\r\ndj48ZGl2PmBgYDwvZGl2PjxkaXY+PGRpdj5kYXQgJmx0Oy0gZGF0YS5mcmFtZShJRCA9IGMoMSwg\r\nMiwgMywgNCwgNSksPC9kaXY+PGRpdj4mbmJzcDsgJm5ic3A7ICZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDsgJm5ic3A7\r\nICZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDsgJm5ic3A7ICZuYnNwOyBWMSA9IHJlcCg1LCA1KSw8L2Rpdj48ZGl2PiZu\r\nYnNwOyAmbmJzcDsgJm5ic3A7ICZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDsgJm5ic3A7ICZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDsgJm5i\r\nc3A7IFYyID0gcmVwKDcsIDUpLDwvZGl2PjxkaXY+Jm5ic3A7ICZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDsgJm5ic3A7\r\nICZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDsgJm5ic3A7ICZuYnNwOyAmbmJzcDsgVjMgPSByZXAoNiwgNSkpPC9kaXY+\r\nPC9kaXY+PGRpdj5gYGA8L2Rpdj48ZGl2PkkgbmVlZCB0byBtYWtlIHNldmVyYWwgZGlmZmVyZW50\r\nIHZlcnNpb25zIG9mIHRoaXMgZGF0YSBmcmFtZSwgZWFjaCB3aXRoIG9uZSBjb2x1bW4gY2hhbmdl\r\nZCB0byBhIGRpZmZlcmVudCB2YWx1ZSAoYWxsIHZhbHVlcyBpbiB0aGUgY29sdW1uIHN0aWxsIGlk\r\nZW50aWNhbCkuICZuYnNwO0kgaGF2ZSBhIHZlY3RvciBsaXN0aW5nIHRoZSBuYW1lcyBvZiB0aGUg\r\nY29sdW1ucyB0byBiZSBjaGFuZ2VkLCBhbmQgYSB2ZWN0b3IgbGlzdGluZyB0aGUgbmV3IHZhbHVl\r\ncyBmb3IgZWFjaCBjb2x1bW4uPC9kaXY+PGRpdj48YnI+PC9kaXY+PGRpdj5gYGA8L2Rpdj48ZGl2\r\nPmNvbC5uYW1lcyAmbHQ7LSBjKCJWMSIsICJWMyIpP